---
import FreeToolNote from '../../components/FreeToolNote.astro';
import LastReviewed from '../../components/LastReviewed.astro';
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import ScoreHistory from '../../components/ScoreHistory.astro';
import SharedResults from '../../components/SharedResults.astro';
import FivePartInterpretation from '../../components/interpretation/FivePartQuestionnaire.astro';
import { FAQ, FAQ_ORDER } from '../../tools/five-part-questionnaire.content';

const items = [
	{ id: 'q1', text: 'Can you now (or could you ever) place your hands flat on the floor without bending your knees?' },
	{ id: 'q2', text: 'Can you now (or could you ever) bend your thumb to touch your forearm?' },
	{ id: 'q3', text: 'As a child, did you amuse your friends by contorting your body into strange shapes, or could you do the splits?' },
	{ id: 'q4', text: 'As a child or teenager, did your shoulder or kneecap dislocate on more than one occasion?' },
	{ id: 'q5', text: 'Do you consider yourself “double-jointed”?' },
];

const faqs = FAQ_ORDER.map(k => FAQ[k]);

// Shown under the heading and used as the sitemap lastmod.
const lastReviewed = '2026-10-16';
---

<Page
	breadcrumb="Five-part questionnaire (5PQ)"
	faqs={faqs}
	title="Five-part questionnaire (5PQ): free hypermobility screen"
	description="Free five-part hypermobility questionnaire (5PQ) with an instant score, no sign-up. Five yes or no questions that catch past hypermobility Beighton misses."
>
			<div class="tool-header">
				<a href="/tools/" class="section-label tools">Tools</a>
				<h1>Five-part questionnaire for hypermobility (5PQ)</h1>
				<LastReviewed date={lastReviewed} />
				<FreeToolNote />
				<p class="subtitle">Five yes/no questions that pick up hypermobility, including hypermobility you used to have</p>
				<p class="description">
					The five-part questionnaire was published by Alan Hakim and Rodney Grahame in 2003 as a quick way to identify generalised joint hypermobility without a physical examination. It asks five yes/no questions, and <strong>two or more "yes" answers</strong> is a positive screen. In the original study of 212 hypermobile women attending London clinics and 57 healthy volunteers it had a sensitivity of <strong>84%</strong> and a specificity of <strong>89%</strong>; a second clinic group gave 84% and 80%. <!-- REVIEW: wording checked against the Hakim and Grahame 2003 abstract -->
				</p>
				<p class="description">
					Its particular value is the phrase <em>"or could you ever"</em>. The <a href="/tools/beighton-score/">Beighton score</a> measures joint range today, and joints stiffen with age, injury, and surgery. Someone who was markedly hypermobile at 20 can fail the Beighton cut-off at 45. The 5PQ captures that history, which is why the 2017 hEDS criteria use it: if your Beighton score is exactly one point below the Beighton cut-off for your group, a positive 5PQ makes up the difference for Criterion 1. <!-- REVIEW: trimmed an unsourced clause -->
				</p>
				<p class="description">
					It takes under a minute. If you screen positive, the next steps are the <a href="/tools/beighton-score/">Beighton score</a> for today's joint range and, if hEDS is a question, the <a href="/tools/heds-criteria/">2017 hEDS criteria checker</a>, which uses both.
				</p>
			</div>

			<form id="fpq-form" novalidate>
				<p class="form-instructions">Answer each question <strong>yes</strong> or <strong>no</strong>. "Could you ever" means at any point in your life, not just now.</p>
				{items.map((item, i) => (
					<div class="symptom" data-id={item.id}>
						<p class="symptom-text"><span class="num">{i + 1}.</span> {item.text}</p>
						<div class="segmented">
							<label><input type="radio" name={item.id} value="1" /><span>Yes</span></label>
							<label><input type="radio" name={item.id} value="0" /><span>No</span></label>
						</div>
					</div>
				))}
				<div class="form-footer">
					<button type="submit">See my result</button>
					<button type="button" id="reset-btn">Clear all</button>
				</div>
			</form>

			<div id="results" class="results" hidden>
				<h2>Your 5PQ result</h2>
				<div class="total-score">
					<span id="total-score-value">—</span>
					<span class="total-score-label">of 5 answered "yes"</span>
				</div>
				<p id="score-interpretation" class="score-interp"></p>
				<p id="positives" class="positives"></p>

				<div class="results-disclaimer">
					<!-- REVIEW: accuracy figures and the hEDS rule moved to the "Understanding your 5PQ score" section below -->
					<p>If you have not measured your Beighton score, the <a href="/tools/beighton-score/">illustrated Beighton tool</a> takes a few minutes. The <a href="/tools/heds-criteria/">hEDS criteria checker</a> then applies both scores together with the rest of the criteria. If you also have symptoms on standing, the <a href="/tools/nasa-lean-test/">NASA lean test</a> and the <a href="/tools/compass-31/">COMPASS-31</a> cover the autonomic side.</p>
					<p><strong>This is not a diagnosis.</strong> Discuss your results with your doctor.</p>
				</div>

				<ScoreHistory toolId="five-part-questionnaire" toolName="5PQ" />

				<button type="button" id="back-btn" class="back-btn">Edit answers</button>
			</div>

			<SharedResults toolId="five-part-questionnaire" />

			<FivePartInterpretation>
				<div class="disclaimer" slot="disclaimer"><strong>This is not a diagnostic tool.</strong> A positive screen suggests generalised joint hypermobility is likely; it does not diagnose hypermobile EDS, a hypermobility spectrum disorder, or anything else. The original studies were in women attending hypermobility clinics, and later studies outside clinics found lower specificity (75% in Swedish adults, 62% in pregnant women), so false positives are common. It has not been validated in children. Discuss your result with your doctor.</div>
				<p class="citation" slot="citation">Based on: Hakim AJ, Grahame R. <em>A simple questionnaire to detect hypermobility: an adjunct to the assessment of patients with diffuse musculoskeletal pain.</em> Int J Clin Pract. 2003;57(3):163–166.</p>
			</FivePartInterpretation>
</Page>

<script>
import { fivePartQuestionnaire } from '../../tools/five-part-questionnaire';
import { mountScoreHistory, mountSharedResults } from '../../scripts/results/scoreHistory';
import { interpretResult } from '../../scripts/results/interpretation';

const history = mountScoreHistory(fivePartQuestionnaire);
mountSharedResults(fivePartQuestionnaire);

const ITEMS = [
	{ id: 'q1', short: 'Hands flat on the floor, knees straight (now or ever)' },
	{ id: 'q2', short: 'Thumb to forearm (now or ever)' },
	{ id: 'q3', short: 'Contortions or the splits as a child' },
	{ id: 'q4', short: 'Shoulder or kneecap dislocated more than once as a child or teenager' },
	{ id: 'q5', short: 'Consider yourself double-jointed' },
];

const form = document.getElementById('fpq-form') as HTMLFormElement;
const results = document.getElementById('results') as HTMLElement;

function getVal(id: string): number | null {
	const checked = form.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(`input[name="${id}"]:checked`);
	return checked ? parseInt(checked.value, 10) : null;
}

form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
	e.preventDefault();
	for (const item of ITEMS) {
		if (getVal(item.id) === null) {
			const el = form.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`.symptom[data-id="${item.id}"]`);
			el?.classList.add('missing');
			el?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
			setTimeout(() => el?.classList.remove('missing'), 2500);
			return;
		}
	}
	const yes = ITEMS.filter(it => getVal(it.id) === 1);
	const n = yes.length;
	(document.getElementById('total-score-value') as HTMLElement).textContent = String(n);

	// REVIEW: Layer 1 copy. The band sentence comes from the tool config via
	// interpretResult; the page adds what the band means.
	const subscores = Object.fromEntries(ITEMS.map(it => [it.id, getVal(it.id) ?? 0]));
	let follow: string;
	if (n >= 2) {
		follow = 'It suggests that a Beighton assessment and, if you have symptoms, a clinical hypermobility assessment are worthwhile. Outside clinics false positives are common, and on its own it is not a diagnosis of any condition.';
	} else if (n === 1) {
		follow = 'A single "yes" does not indicate generalised hypermobility, though it does not rule out hypermobility in particular joints.';
	} else {
		follow = 'Generalised joint hypermobility is unlikely on this measure. If a clinician has raised hypermobility with you, the Beighton score is the next step regardless.';
	}
	(document.getElementById('score-interpretation') as HTMLElement).textContent =
		[interpretResult(fivePartQuestionnaire, { total: n, subscores }, history.latest()), follow].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
	(document.getElementById('positives') as HTMLElement).innerHTML = yes.length
		? `<strong>Items answered yes:</strong> ${yes.map(y => y.short).join('; ')}.`
		: '';

	try {
		localStorage.setItem('pvr-5pq-result', JSON.stringify({ date: new Date().toISOString(), yes: n, answers: Object.fromEntries(ITEMS.map(it => [it.id, getVal(it.id)])) }));
	} catch { /* storage unavailable */ }

	history.record({ total: n, subscores });

	form.hidden = true;
	results.hidden = false;
	results.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
});

document.getElementById('reset-btn')?.addEventListener('click', () => form.reset());
document.getElementById('back-btn')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
	results.hidden = true;
	form.hidden = false;
	form.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
});
</script>

<style>
	.tool-header { padding-bottom: 1.5em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); margin-bottom: 2em; }
	.tool-header h1 { margin: 0.3em 0 0.1em; }
	.subtitle { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 1.05em; margin: 0 0 0.75em; }
	.description { margin-bottom: 1em; }

	.form-instructions { font-size: 0.88em; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); border-radius: 3px; padding: 0.7em 1.1em; margin-bottom: 1.25em;
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}

	.symptom { border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); padding: 0.9em 0; margin-bottom: 0.65em; transition: border-color 0.15s, box-shadow 0.15s; }
	.symptom.missing { border-color: #c0392b; box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(192, 57, 43, 0.12); }
	.symptom-text { margin: 0 0 0.7em; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.4; }
	.num { color: rgb(var(--gray)); margin-right: 0.3em; }

	.segmented { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 0.3em; max-width: 16em; }
	.segmented label { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.88em; padding: 0.45em 0; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; transition: background 0.1s, border-color 0.1s; }
	.segmented label:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
	.segmented input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; width: 0; height: 0; }
	.segmented label:has(input:checked) { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; font-weight: 700; }

	.form-footer { display: flex; gap: 1em; padding: 1.5em 0 1em; }
	button[type="submit"] { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; border: none; padding: 0.75em 2em; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 1em; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; }
	button[type="submit"]:hover { background: var(--accent-dark); }
	button[type="button"] { background: none; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); padding: 0.75em 1.5em; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.95em; cursor: pointer; color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-family: inherit; }

	.results { padding-top: 1em; }
	.results h2 { margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
	.results h3 { margin-top: 1.75em; margin-bottom: 0.4em; }
	.total-score { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.5em; margin: 1em 0; }
	#total-score-value { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 3.2em; font-weight: 600; color: rgb(var(--black)); line-height: 1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
	.total-score-label { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 1.1em; }
	.score-interp { font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1em; padding: 0; }
	.positives { font-size: 0.92em; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); }

	.results-disclaimer { font-size: 0.88em; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); padding-top: 1.5em; margin-top: 2em; line-height: 1.6; }
	.results-disclaimer h3 { font-size: 1em; color: rgb(var(--black)); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
	.results-disclaimer a { color: var(--accent); }
	.back-btn { background: none; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); padding: 0.6em 1.25em; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.95em; cursor: pointer; color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-family: inherit; margin-top: 1.5em; }
	.back-btn:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }

	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.symptom { padding: 0.8em 0; }
	}
</style>
